.TH SDL_TouchFingerEvent 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_TouchFingerEvent \- Touch finger event structure (event.tfinger.*)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_events.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_TouchFingerEvent
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_EventType type; /**< SDL_EVENT_FINGER_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_FINGER_UP, SDL_EVENT_FINGER_MOTION, or SDL_EVENT_FINGER_CANCELED */
.BI "    Uint32 reserved;
.BI "    Uint64 timestamp;   /**< In nanoseconds, populated using SDL_GetTicksNS() */
.BI "    SDL_TouchID touchID; /**< The touch device id */
.BI "    SDL_FingerID fingerID;
.BI "    float x;            /**< Normalized in the range 0...1 */
.BI "    float y;            /**< Normalized in the range 0...1 */
.BI "    float dx;           /**< Normalized in the range -1...1 */
.BI "    float dy;           /**< Normalized in the range -1...1 */
.BI "    float pressure;     /**< Normalized in the range 0...1 */
.BI "    SDL_WindowID windowID; /**< The window underneath the finger, if any */
.BI "} SDL_TouchFingerEvent;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Coordinates in this event are normalized\[char46]
.BR x
and
.BR y
are normalized to a range between 0\[char46]0f and 1\[char46]0f, relative to the window, so (0,0) is the top left and (1,1) is the bottom right\[char46] Delta coordinates
.BR dx
and
.BR dy
are normalized in the ranges of -1\[char46]0f (traversed all the way from the bottom or right to all the way up or left) to 1\[char46]0f (traversed all the way from the top or left to all the way down or right)\[char46]
.PP
Note that while the coordinates are _normalized_, they are not _clamped_, which means in some circumstances you can get a value outside of this range\[char46] For example, a renderer using logical presentation might give a negative value when the touch is in the letterboxing\[char46] Some platforms might report a touch outside of the window, which will also be outside of the range\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

